00:15:02.780 --> 00:15:03.880
He's a demon king.

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:05.900
Why doesn't he just keep you in the torture room?

00:15:06.060 --> 00:15:07.860
Why does he just keep you there in the torture room forever, then?

00:15:07.860 --> 00:15:09.460
Well, I mean, like, you know, there's a...

00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:10.920
He's Beezlebutt. Beezlebutt.

00:15:10.980 --> 00:15:15.460
There's a timer. He said, you know, he's like...

00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:17.120
Oh, I said the word.

00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:20.600
Sorry, guys. I probably have bleeped that out, honestly.

00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:23.940
I probably have... He said the bad home assistant word.

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:25.240
Yeah, he said the home assistant word.

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:28.260
But, yeah, he probably was like, you know, said timer for...

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:29.140
How many times has he jumped?

00:15:29.600 --> 00:15:37.160
45. It's such a crazy complicated way of going about, like, torturing the player.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:38.840
Yeah. It's not torturing him.

00:15:38.940 --> 00:15:40.000
It's you. You the player.

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:41.740
Don't have fun playing this game.

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:44.080
Here's the thing, though, Sean, that confuses me.

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:48.820
When would you collect more than nine of these mighty coins?

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:52.100
Well, when you're like me and you don't know how to activate them.

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:54.840
Okay. You just sort of accrue them over time.

00:15:55.220 --> 00:16:03.500
Yeah. And if you're like me and you activate them on accident, you're just completely confused about what's happening because you haven't read the manual yet.

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:07.140
And you've just changed your skin color and everything.

00:16:07.140 --> 00:16:09.140
And you're the color of your clothes.

00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:11.800
And, you know, that was like...

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:14.120
I was like, okay, nothing feels different.

00:16:14.420 --> 00:16:16.900
You know, like, I don't have a new attack or something.

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:19.560
No, Mike. Now you can open the orange boxes.

00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:20.400
Well, yeah.

00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:21.960
So that's the thing.

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:26.640
Okay. This is confusing because let me walk you through the powers.

00:16:26.980 --> 00:16:28.380
You have blue.

00:16:29.100 --> 00:16:30.140
You have orange.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:31.460
And then you have green.

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:33.700
Those are your suits that you can change into.

00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:37.540
And it would be really obvious if it was like, oh, yeah, blue.

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:39.320
That lets you open up the blue chest.

00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:41.700
Orange. That lets you open up the harder chest.

00:16:41.820 --> 00:16:43.200
The orange chest. You know, green.

00:16:43.420 --> 00:16:44.480
Now you get the green chest, right?

00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:45.840
It's like, no. Okay.

00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:49.620
Blue allows you to open the orange treasure boxes.

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:57.640
Orange allows you to open the orange and red boxes, but also allowing them to open by simply touching them from the side.

00:16:57.840 --> 00:17:01.640
So there's a couple levels where that's like a puzzle aspect to it.

00:17:01.940 --> 00:17:08.220
And then there's green, which just turns all the enemies on screen into gold coins for five seconds.

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:10.360
It's a great mechanic.

00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:18.340
I mean, it's not, but I genuinely want to ask you how far into this game you played.

00:17:18.700 --> 00:17:19.880
Yeah, I got far.

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:21.080
You did? Yes. Yeah, yeah.

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:22.900
This game was not hard for me at all.

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:25.420
I don't even, I'm not even talking about difficulty.

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:29.280
I'm talking about just like maintaining your level of attention.

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:33.280
To be honest, I just wanted to see if there was like variety.

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:34.780
Yeah. Was there any?

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:36.280
So here's the thing.

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:39.320
You know, they do do some creative things with the chests.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:42.360
Okay. You know, and like using the power-ups and stuff.

00:17:42.860 --> 00:17:46.860
But no. There's really not enough change going on.

00:17:46.980 --> 00:17:49.240
It doesn't get any harder either necessarily.

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:54.720
Like, yeah, more enemies might be harder, but still it's a game of dodging, not of attacking.

00:17:54.720 --> 00:18:01.020
So more enemies on the screen just makes it like, okay, that's the area I must avoid for now.

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:02.760
Like, let me hang back here.

00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:08.040
They'll crawl over to me at snail's pace and then I'll jump over them all.

00:18:08.180 --> 00:18:09.200
You know, it's like, all right.

00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:38.800
So is there any, is there any progression in the story as far as you got?

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:39.980
As far as I got, no.

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:46.920
No. Because that's a lot of, that's a lot of description for a game that doesn't seem to have much to talk about.

00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:51.540
In terms of like, it has a pretty intense story in the manual.

00:18:51.720 --> 00:18:52.780
Right. That I would think.

00:18:53.120 --> 00:18:56.600
Here is the cool thing though, about the story at least.

00:18:56.840 --> 00:18:59.520
Is that there are multiple endings.

00:18:59.940 --> 00:19:01.080
I did see that.

00:19:01.300 --> 00:19:02.460
Yeah. That's pretty cool.

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:04.620
This is our first NES game.

00:19:04.900 --> 00:19:06.840
Probably one of the only NES games we're going to get.

00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:09.100
Where your choices matter.

00:19:09.740 --> 00:19:16.740
And basically it's all dependent on what conditions the player has satisfied before entering the final series of rooms.

00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:24.060
And, you know, not that it's like, there's no dialogue choices or that or like saving, you know.

00:19:24.460 --> 00:19:28.040
No, at the top is a morality slider.

00:19:28.360 --> 00:19:33.740
Right, right, right. It's like, did Jack even want to save his brothers or did he want to become king?

00:19:35.140 --> 00:19:36.900
King Mighty Jack, the sequel.

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:46.980
No. Instead, the best ending can be done by getting both crystal balls, there are two, and the five secret coins.

00:19:46.980 --> 00:19:54.300
So that's kind of why you want to, you know, explore the level and collect the things that I told you not to do.

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:56.520
Because you're not going to find that stuff otherwise.

00:19:56.940 --> 00:20:02.120
Yeah. I will say, another thing about the level design in general was that I didn't think it was very creative.

00:20:02.580 --> 00:20:06.840
No. I thought that, you know, the puzzle aspects were probably the best part.

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:09.960
And that it was nice to have like some secrets.

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:14.040
Yeah. Like some little places to like drop down to and find things.

00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:22.640
Mm-hmm. But other than that, like not a lot going on here in terms of like, you know, well, this stage has to look like this.

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:26.260
So this way the enemies, when they spawn here, it's like, it's not that well thought out.

00:20:26.460 --> 00:20:29.340
No. It's just kind of like enemies will spawn wherever they want.

00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:35.260
And there's sort of like a path that you can kind of see that the bombs make is the optimal path.

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:36.400
Right. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:20:36.400 --> 00:20:42.560
And it's like, okay, it's kind of like, it's like a less, well, it's like a less well-designed version of the coins in Super Mario Bros.

00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:45.440
kind of outlining where you should jump and do stuff like that.

00:20:45.880 --> 00:20:50.800
But if you do happen to get the best ending, it just allows you to save the entire family.

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:52.000
So that's cool.

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:53.080
That's fun. You know?

00:20:53.780 --> 00:20:59.160
Basically, if you don't do that, the other endings, it's like, there's almost everyone's here.

00:20:59.580 --> 00:21:01.740
But you left someone behind, Jack.

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:04.200
Which is weird. Damn it, Jack.

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:07.880
So yeah, there's that.

00:21:08.980 --> 00:21:13.400
And secret coins, by the way, can only be picked up while you're in the green form.

00:21:13.740 --> 00:21:15.540
So that's important to note, too.

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:21.160
Because you might just look through this whole level and be like, I've been searching this damn level for hours.

00:21:21.220 --> 00:21:25.220
Whereas these secret coins, they're only available in the green form.

00:21:25.220 --> 00:21:37.900
I will say, though, that I had been playing some more intense, anxiety-inducing games before I started playing this one.

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:40.020
And it's a nice reprieve.

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:43.000
It's a more relaxing experience.

00:21:43.480 --> 00:21:47.120
Because I do think that the jump feels good, unlike you.

00:21:47.120 --> 00:21:54.200
So moving around is enjoyable to some extent.

00:21:55.440 --> 00:21:58.800
But yeah, I didn't feel like I had to do much.

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:00.160
There's not much direction.

00:22:00.680 --> 00:22:01.640
Right. Yeah.

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:13.680
I think, like, for me, with this game, there's enough to appreciate when it comes to, like, secrets and the multiple endings thing is cool.

00:22:13.680 --> 00:22:15.680
And the jump thing you told me about is cool.

00:22:15.720 --> 00:22:17.560
And I'm definitely going to go back and try that out.

00:22:17.580 --> 00:22:20.620
Because it's just weird that I never thought to press A again.

00:22:20.620 --> 00:22:25.580
Yeah, like, you know, I guess that makes sense, though, if you really think about, like, why would I jump again while I'm jumping?

00:22:26.080 --> 00:22:27.700
But, you know, I think that stuff is cool.

00:22:28.060 --> 00:22:33.720
But overall, like, you know, the game is just, like, it's not tight enough.

00:22:33.940 --> 00:22:37.000
No. And it's not, there's really no difficulty either.

00:22:37.140 --> 00:22:41.320
I'm really surprised about this, that we have an NES game that's actually, like, kind of easy.

00:22:41.560 --> 00:22:42.720
Yeah, a little too easy.

00:22:43.080 --> 00:22:48.200
This game feels like it was made by Game Maker.

00:22:48.240 --> 00:22:50.020
Like, it was made in Game Maker.

00:22:50.020 --> 00:22:52.660
And they didn't know how to really get...

00:22:52.660 --> 00:23:01.680
Be nice. I just, because of how freeform it feels, because you can just go wherever you want.

00:23:01.680 --> 00:23:06.340
There's no real, like, failure states except for bumping into an enemy.

00:23:06.560 --> 00:23:08.200
I don't know. I hear you.

00:23:08.440 --> 00:23:14.400
No crap. I mean, you know, Mighty Bomb Jack is the sequel to Bomb Jack.

00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:15.940
So... Oh, yeah, I remember.

00:23:16.240 --> 00:23:20.080
Yeah, yeah, yeah. I'm telling you, like, the game does have a following.

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:27.200
But Bomb Jack was weird in the sense that, like, it had a huge focus on, like, an Egyptian theme.

00:23:27.680 --> 00:23:31.840
Oh. Like, with, like, sphinxes and pyramids.

00:23:31.840 --> 00:23:35.900
And, yes, there's a sphinx in the game, too, for Mighty Bomb Jack.

00:23:36.180 --> 00:23:41.820
But, like, it was just, like, really weird how, like, they swapped in those backgrounds.

00:23:41.820 --> 00:23:44.360
And it doesn't really look arcade-like at all.

00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:47.260
It looks kind of like an Amiga game.

00:23:47.420 --> 00:23:48.820
Yeah, was that... You know, like a computer game.

00:23:48.820 --> 00:23:54.460
So, Mike just showed me a picture that actually had the sphinx in it.

00:23:54.580 --> 00:23:56.040
Was that from the arcade version?

00:23:56.220 --> 00:23:59.500
Yeah, that's from the arcade version of just regular Bomb Jack, to be clear.

00:23:59.760 --> 00:24:04.560
And now this one is just, like, a very normal palette of walls.

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:05.880
Yes, exactly.

00:24:05.880 --> 00:24:10.880
Yeah, this one seems to be a little more, like, grounded in what other NES games were doing at the time.

00:24:10.940 --> 00:24:16.580
And not trying to do, like, photorealistic sphinxes and stuff like that.

00:24:16.580 --> 00:24:19.160
Yeah, the game did get plenty of ports, though.

00:24:19.320 --> 00:24:23.160
I mean, it definitely went to the Amiga and other PC-related stuff.

00:24:23.620 --> 00:24:26.160
It got a port on the Game Boy, too.

00:24:26.460 --> 00:24:28.520
Just Bomb Jack, not Mighty Bomb Jack.

00:24:29.000 --> 00:24:36.280
So, it's out there if you're interested in checking out the Bomb Jack line of Bomb Jack, Bomb Jack 2, and Mighty Bomb Jack.

